id: pm-rl-yxhe
title: "The changelog heading records the day it was generated, so the gate fails every following day"
description: "Two clock dependencies in the release gate. The lockfile pinned a pm-changelog older than 2026.8.2, which derived release dates in local time, so a host at a positive UTC offset and a UTC runner disagreed about the date. The one that actually bit this package: it is release-gated and therefore has no tags, and without a tag pm-changelog falls back to the current date for the release heading. The committed heading recorded the day it happened to be generated rather than the date the version encodes, so changelog:check compared against a freshly generated heading and failed on every subsequent day. The check was already failing when this was found, with no change to the tracker or the code. Every released package in this fleet pairs a CalVer version with its matching date, so the generated heading was inconsistent with that convention as well as unstable."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: "area:release",dependencies,pm-changelog
created_at: "2026-08-03T07:13:46.369Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T07:13:46.369Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "The lockfile resolves pm-changelog to 2026.8.2 or newer; the three changelog scripts pass an explicit release date rather than relying on the fallback; the committed heading pairs the version with the date that version encodes; changelog:check passes today and passes again under a timezone a day behind this host, so its result does not depend on when it runs"
body: ""
